"""
Forbidden City — Palace Museum, Beijing (Q80290) — the walled palace, its moat, gates, corner towers, halls,
courtyards and gardens, built by code.

Author: Álvaro C. Chulvi (with AI assistance). Licence of the resulting model: CC BY 4.0.
The monument: the imperial palace of the Ming and Qing dynasties, built 1406–1420 for the Yongle Emperor
(master builder Kuai Xiang, died 1481, among others), rebuilt in parts after fires up to the 18th–19th centuries
(the present Hall of Supreme Harmony dates from 1695–1697). Public domain.

What is modelled:
- The moat (Tongzi He, 52 m wide) with its stone banks, the strip of paving between the moat and the wall.
- The purple-red city wall (10 m, 8.6 m thick at the base, 6.7 m at the top) with its crenellated outer parapet
  and low inner parapet, the four corner towers (jiaolou: cross plan, porches with hip-and-gable roofs on all
  four sides, two crossing hip-and-gable roofs on top and a gilded finial), the Meridian Gate (Wumen) with its
  U-shaped red platform, five tunnels, main hall (double-eaved hip roof), wing galleries and four pavilions,
  the Gate of Divine Prowess (Shenwumen) on the north side, the East and West Glorious Gates (Donghuamen,
  Xihuamen) on their red platforms with their ramps.
- The Outer Court: the Gate of Supreme Harmony with its marble platform and the Inner Golden Water River in a
  bow in front of it with its five marble bridges; the three-tiered white marble terrace (8.13 m) with its
  balustrades, stairs and the carved ramps on the axis; the Hall of Supreme Harmony (double-eaved hip roof,
  35.05 m), the Hall of Central Harmony (pyramidal roof, gilded finial), the Hall of Preserving Harmony
  (double-eaved hip-and-gable roof); the side halls, belvederes, gates and corner towers of the great squares.
- The Inner Court: the Gate of Heavenly Purity, the Palace of Heavenly Purity, the Hall of Union, the Palace of
  Earthly Tranquility on their marble platforms, the Imperial Garden with its pavilions and old cypresses,
  and the six western and six eastern palaces, the Palace of Tranquil Longevity, the Hall of Mental
  Cultivation, the Palace of Compassion and Tranquility, the Hall of Military Prowess, the Hall of Literary
  Glory and every other hall, gate, corridor and courtyard wall that OpenStreetMap draws (~1,000 outlines),
  each with a marble or brick platform, red walls and columns, a blue-green painted bracket band under the
  eaves and a roof of the right kind.
- The roofs: a generic Chinese-roof builder — hip (wudian), hip-and-gable (xieshan) with its red gable,
  gable (yingshan), pyramidal (zanjian) with a gilded finial; single or double eaves; the slopes concave
  (steep at the ridge, flat at the eaves) and the eaves curving up and out at the corners; ridges, hip ridges
  and ridge-end ornaments (chiwen) on the main halls. Imperial yellow glazed tiles everywhere except the green
  roofs of the Southern Three Lodges, the black ones of the Wenyuan Pavilion and grey service houses.
- Not modelled: interiors, the ceramic beasts on the ridges, the bronze lions, cranes, cauldrons and sundials,
  the Duanmen and Tiananmen to the south (outside the moat), the streets and the terrain.

Measurements (see meta.json for the sources):
- Plan: OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL): relation 9511883 (the Forbidden City, its wall as
  ways 638176319, 1341826249, 638252480, 1341826250), the moat (way 4845030), ~1,080 building outlines and the
  ~700 building:parts of the detailed 3D mapping of the main halls (relations 8854043 Hall of Supreme Harmony,
  8854507 Hall of Preserving Harmony, 8851737 Gate of Supreme Harmony, 8849989 Meridian Gate, 8858781 Gate of
  Divine Prowess, 8858938 East Glorious Gate, 8858329 / 8858355 SE and NE corner towers, 8860936 / 8860927 /
  8861202 the three rear palaces, …), the terrace tiers (ways 638449443/4/8, 638467898–900, relations
  8854307–8854309), the Inner Golden Water River (ways 638204006, 685378549 …) and its bridges, the walls
  (barrier=wall), woods and gardens and 87 mapped trees. All in the axes of heading 177.89° (the city is
  turned ~2.1° anticlockwise from true north, as the whole Beijing axis).
  OSM lacks the west wall's corner towers and the West Glorious Gate: they are mirrored from the east ones
  (the palace is symmetric about its axis; the west gate's position is uncertain by ±10 m).
- Size: the wall 961 × 753 m (en.wikipedia), here 962 × 752 m from OSM; moat 52 m wide (en.wikipedia).
- Heights: city wall 10 m (zh.wikipedia: 城墙高约10米; base 8.62 m, top 6.66 m wide, en.wikipedia), corner
  towers 27.5 m to the finial (the usual figure, ±5 %), Meridian Gate: platform 12.00 m, gate tower 60.05 × 25 m
  (zh.wikipedia 午门), 37.95 m in all (the usual figure), Gate of Divine Prowess 31 m (zh.wikipedia 神武门), Gate
  of Supreme Harmony 23.8 m (zh.wikipedia 故宫) on a ~3.4 m platform (estimate), three-tiered terrace 8.13 m,
  Hall of Supreme Harmony 26.92 m above the terrace / 35.05 m in all, 63.96 × 37 m with its base (zh.wikipedia
  太和殿), Hall of Preserving Harmony 29.5 m (zh.wikipedia 保和殿), Hall of Central Harmony ~27 m (estimate,
  ±10 %), East and West Glorious Gates ~26.5 m (OSM, ±10 %). The other
  heights come from the OSM building:parts, whose heights run 16–19 % above the published figures of the halls
  above (41 m for 35.05, 35 for 29.5, 29 for 23.8, 45 for 37.95), so they are scaled by 0.84 (±10 %); the
  marble platforms by 0.9 (9 m for 8.13). Buildings without heights in OSM get one from their depth (eaves
  2.6 m + 0.2 × depth, roof rise 0.3 × depth; ±20 %).
Colours: imperial yellow glazed tiles, vermilion walls and columns, purple-red palace and city walls,
blue-green painted brackets, white marble terraces and balustrades, grey brick paving, the moat and river water.

Axes (docs/MODEL_SPEC.md): +Y up, the Meridian Gate (south) faces +Z, heading 177.89°; +X points to 87.89°
(east). Origin on the ground at the centre of the walled rectangle (the middle of the four corners of the wall).

    python model_sources/Q80290_forbidden_city.py   -> models/Q80290/model.glb (+ triangles and footprint in meta.json)
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import json
import math
import sys
from pathlib import Path

import numpy as np

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / "tools"))
from meshkit import Mesh, merge, box, cyl, lathe, tube, cap, walls, extrude, offset, triangulate, ring_area, normals, write_glb  # noqa: E402

rng = np.random.default_rng(1420)
HEADING = 177.89

# ── Colours ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
YELLOW = (0.86, 0.64, 0.17)          # imperial yellow glazed tiles
YELLOW_D = (0.72, 0.50, 0.12)        # ridges
GREEN_T = (0.27, 0.48, 0.34)         # green glazed tiles
BLACK_T = (0.19, 0.20, 0.21)         # black glazed tiles (Wenyuan Ge)
GREY_T = (0.42, 0.43, 0.44)          # grey tiles of the service houses
RED = (0.66, 0.17, 0.12)             # vermilion walls and columns
RED_D = (0.44, 0.11, 0.08)           # lattice doors and windows
WALL_RED = (0.56, 0.20, 0.17)        # purple-red palace and city walls
TEAL = (0.17, 0.37, 0.40)            # painted brackets and beams under the eaves
GABLE = (0.60, 0.16, 0.12)           # red gables of the hip-and-gable roofs
MARBLE = (0.90, 0.89, 0.85)
MARBLE_D = (0.79, 0.78, 0.74)
STONE = (0.68, 0.67, 0.64)
BRICK = (0.52, 0.52, 0.51)           # grey brick: the top of the wall, the merlons
PAVE = (0.60, 0.59, 0.56)            # grey brick paving of the courtyards
PAVE_L = (0.76, 0.75, 0.71)          # the stone Imperial Way on the axis
WATER = (0.29, 0.41, 0.42)
LEAF = (0.22, 0.34, 0.17)
LEAF_L = (0.30, 0.42, 0.20)
GRASS = (0.40, 0.47, 0.27)
GOLD = (0.86, 0.68, 0.24)
DARK = (0.09, 0.07, 0.06)

S_OSM = 0.84                          # OSM building:part heights -> published heights (see the docstring)
S_STONE = 8.13 / 9.0                  # OSM marble platforms (the 9 m terrace is 8.13 m)
FOUND = -2.5


def sc(c, k=0.035):
    return tuple(np.clip(np.asarray(c) * (1 + rng.normal(0, k)), 0, 1))


def B(x0, x1, y0, y1, z0, z1, c):
    """A box between the given planes, without its bottom face (it always stands on something)."""
    m = box(x1 - x0, y1 - y0, z1 - z0, c).T((x0 + x1) / 2, y0, (z0 + z1) / 2)
    m.f = m.f[:10]
    return m


def place(m, a, cx, cz):
    """Turn a mesh built in local axes (long side along x) by a (radians, local x -> (cos a, sin a)) and move it."""
    c, s = math.cos(a), math.sin(a)
    x, z = m.v[:, 0].copy(), m.v[:, 2].copy()
    m.v[:, 0] = x * c - z * s + cx
    m.v[:, 2] = x * s + z * c + cz
    return m


def face_up(m):
    """Flip the faces of a surface so that it faces up."""
    if len(m.f):
        a, b, c = m.v[m.f[:, 0]], m.v[m.f[:, 1]], m.v[m.f[:, 2]]
        if np.cross(b - a, c - a)[:, 1].sum() < 0:
            m.f = m.f[:, ::-1]
    return m


def face_out(m, cx=0.0, cz=0.0):
    if len(m.f):
        a, b, c = m.v[m.f[:, 0]], m.v[m.f[:, 1]], m.v[m.f[:, 2]]
        n = np.cross(b - a, c - a)
        d = (a + b + c) / 3 - np.array([cx, 0, cz])
        if (n[:, 0] * d[:, 0] + n[:, 2] * d[:, 2]).sum() < 0:
            m.f = m.f[:, ::-1]
    return m


def pip(x, z, P):
    c = False
    n = len(P)
    for i in range(n):
        (x0, z0), (x1, z1) = P[i - 1], P[i]
        if (z0 > z) != (z1 > z) and x < x0 + (z - z0) * (x1 - x0) / (z1 - z0):
            c = not c
    return c


def bbox(P):
    P = np.asarray(P, float)
    return P[:, 0].min(), P[:, 0].max(), P[:, 1].min(), P[:, 1].max()


def rect(x0, x1, z0, z1):
    return [(x0, z0), (x1, z0), (x1, z1), (x0, z1)]


# ── Plans: the long axis of an outline, rectangles ──────────────────────────
def axis_of(P):
    """Angle of the long side of the smallest rectangle round P, snapped to the city grid within 4°."""
    P = np.asarray(P, float)
    best = None
    for i in range(len(P)):
        d = P[i] - P[i - 1]
        if np.hypot(*d) < 0.5:
            continue
        a = math.atan2(d[1], d[0])
        c, s = math.cos(a), math.sin(a)
        u = P[:, 0] * c + P[:, 1] * s; v = -P[:, 0] * s + P[:, 1] * c
        A = (u.max() - u.min()) * (v.max() - v.min())
        if best is None or A < best[0]:
            best = (A, a)
    a = best[1] if best else 0.0
    k = round(a / (math.pi / 2))
    if abs(a - k * math.pi / 2) < math.radians(4):
        a = k * math.pi / 2
    return a % math.pi


def to_local(P, a):
    P = np.asarray(P, float)
    c, s = math.cos(a), math.sin(a)
    return np.stack([P[:, 0] * c + P[:, 1] * s, -P[:, 0] * s + P[:, 1] * c], 1)


def from_local(u, v, a):
    c, s = math.cos(a), math.sin(a)
    return u * c - v * s, u * s + v * c


def lrect(P, a):
    """Bounding rectangle of P in the axes turned by a -> (cx, cz, L along a, D across)."""
    Q = to_local(P, a)
    u0, u1, v0, v1 = Q[:, 0].min(), Q[:, 0].max(), Q[:, 1].min(), Q[:, 1].max()
    cx, cz = from_local((u0 + u1) / 2, (v0 + v1) / 2, a)
    return cx, cz, u1 - u0, v1 - v0


def _cluster(vals, tol):
    vals = sorted(vals)
    groups = [[vals[0]]]
    for x in vals[1:]:
        if x - groups[-1][-1] < tol:
            groups[-1].append(x)
        else:
            groups.append([x])
    return [sum(g) / len(g) for g in groups]


def decompose(P, a, tol=0.9):
    """Rectilinear outline -> rectangles (u0, u1, v0, v1) in the axes turned by a (greedy, fewest of two ways)."""
    Q = to_local(P, a)
    us = _cluster(Q[:, 0], tol); vs = _cluster(Q[:, 1], tol)
    snap = lambda x, g: min(g, key=lambda y: abs(y - x))
    R = [(snap(u, us), snap(v, vs)) for u, v in Q]
    nu, nv = len(us) - 1, len(vs) - 1
    if nu < 1 or nv < 1:
        return []
    inside = np.zeros((nu, nv), bool)
    for i in range(nu):
        for j in range(nv):
            inside[i, j] = pip((us[i] + us[i + 1]) / 2, (vs[j] + vs[j + 1]) / 2, R)

    def greedy(ins, U, V):
        used = np.zeros_like(ins)
        out = []
        for j in range(ins.shape[1]):
            for i in range(ins.shape[0]):
                if not ins[i, j] or used[i, j]:
                    continue
                i2 = i
                while i2 + 1 < ins.shape[0] and ins[i2 + 1, j] and not used[i2 + 1, j]:
                    i2 += 1
                j2 = j
                while j2 + 1 < ins.shape[1] and all(ins[k, j2 + 1] and not used[k, j2 + 1] for k in range(i, i2 + 1)):
                    j2 += 1
                used[i:i2 + 1, j:j2 + 1] = True
                out.append((U[i], U[i2 + 1], V[j], V[j2 + 1]))
        return out
    r1 = greedy(inside, us, vs)
    r2 = [(c, d, a_, b_) for a_, b_, c, d in greedy(inside.T, vs, us)]
    rs = r1 if len(r1) <= len(r2) else r2
    return [r for r in rs if min(r[1] - r[0], r[3] - r[2]) > 1.0]


# ── The Chinese roof ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
P_EXP = 1.6


def drop(t):
    """Fraction of the roof rise lost at distance t (0 ridge .. 1 eave) from the ridge: steep at the ridge, flat
    at the eaves (the concave Chinese slope)."""
    return 1 - (1 - t) ** P_EXP


def _rings(hx_f, hz_f, y_f, ts, n, up, out_, t0=0.0):
    rings = []
    for t in ts:
        hx, hz, y = hx_f(t), hz_f(t), y_f(t)
        pts = []
        for s in range(4):
            for i in range(n):
                u = -1 + 2 * i / n
                if s == 0:
                    pts.append((u * hx, y, hz))
                elif s == 1:
                    pts.append((hx, y, -u * hz))
                elif s == 2:
                    pts.append((-u * hx, y, -hz))
                else:
                    pts.append((-hx, y, u * hz))
        R = np.array(pts, float)
        w = ((t - t0) / (1 - t0)) ** 3 if t > t0 else 0.0
        if w > 0:
            cx = np.clip(np.abs(R[:, 0]) / max(hx, 1e-6), 0, 1)
            cz = np.clip(np.abs(R[:, 2]) / max(hz, 1e-6), 0, 1)
            c = (cx * cz) ** 3 * w
            R[:, 1] += up * c
            R[:, 0] += np.sign(R[:, 0]) * out_ * c
            R[:, 2] += np.sign(R[:, 2]) * out_ * c
        rings.append(R)
    return rings


def _sheet(rings, c):
    """Quads between consecutive rings (each the same length, cyclic)."""
    V = np.vstack(rings)
    m = len(rings[0])
    F = []
    for k in range(len(rings) - 1):
        a, b = k * m, (k + 1) * m
        for i in range(m):
            j = (i + 1) % m
            F += [(a + i, b + i, b + j), (a + i, b + j, a + j)]
    return Mesh(V, F, c)


def _drop_degenerate(m):
    if not len(m.f):
        return m
    a, b, c = m.v[m.f[:, 0]], m.v[m.f[:, 1]], m.v[m.f[:, 2]]
    ar = np.linalg.norm(np.cross(b - a, c - a), axis=1)
    m.f = m.f[ar > 1e-6]
    return m


def compact(m):
    """Drop the vertices no face uses (the bottoms of the boxes, collapsed ridges)."""
    used = np.unique(m.f)
    remap = np.full(len(m.v), -1, np.int64)
    remap[used] = np.arange(len(used))
    m.v, m.c, m.f = m.v[used], m.c[used], remap[m.f]
    return m


def _fascia(R, th, c):
    m = _sheet([R, R - np.array([0, th, 0])], c)
    return face_out(m)


def roof(L, D, ye, yr, kind, c, detail=1, up=None, ridge=True, chiwen=False, gable_c=GABLE, fascia=True, tg=0.5):
    """A Chinese roof over an eave rectangle L (x) × D (z), L ≥ D, centred on the origin: eaves at ye, ridge at yr.
    kind: 'wudian' (hip), 'xieshan' (hip-and-gable), 'gable' (yingshan), 'zanjian' (pyramidal). Returns meshes."""
    out = []
    H = max(yr - ye, 0.3)
    hx0, hz0 = L / 2, D / 2
    n = {0: 2, 1: 3, 2: 5}[detail]
    K = {0: 2, 1: 3, 2: 5}[detail]
    if up is None:
        up = float(np.clip(0.045 * D, 0.15, 1.5))
    out_ = up * 0.6
    hr = float(np.clip(0.045 * D, 0.25, 1.4))                  # ridge height
    yf = lambda t: yr - H * drop(t)
    if kind == "gable":
        xs = np.linspace(-hx0, hx0, (max(2, n - 1) if detail else 1) + 1)
        ts = np.linspace(0, 1, K + 1)
        for sgn in (1, -1):
            V, F = [], []
            for t in ts:
                for x in xs:
                    V.append((x, yf(t), sgn * hz0 * t))
            nx = len(xs)
            for k in range(K):
                for i in range(nx - 1):
                    a, b = k * nx + i, (k + 1) * nx + i
                    F += [(a, b, b + 1), (a, b + 1, a + 1)]
            out.append(face_up(Mesh(V, F, c)))
            if fascia and detail:
                e = np.array([(x, ye, sgn * hz0) for x in xs])
                f = Mesh(np.vstack([e, e - [0, min(0.5, 0.06 * D + 0.15), 0]]),
                         [(i, i + 1, nx + i + 1) for i in range(nx - 1)] + [(i, nx + i + 1, nx + i) for i in range(nx - 1)], TEAL)
                out.append(face_out(f))
        for sx in (1, -1):                          # the gable walls, a little inside the verge
            x = sx * (hx0 - 0.25)
            prof = [(sgn * hz0 * t, yf(t)) for sgn in (1,) for t in ts[::-1]] + [(-hz0 * t, yf(t)) for t in ts[1:]]
            V = [(x, ye - 0.6, 0.0)] + [(x, y, z) for z, y in prof]
            F = [(0, i, i + 1) for i in range(1, len(V) - 1)]
            out.append(face_out(Mesh(V, F, gable_c)))
        if ridge:
            out.append(B(-hx0 + 0.1, hx0 - 0.1, yr - hr * 0.35, yr + hr * 0.65, -hr * 0.4, hr * 0.4, YELLOW_D if c == YELLOW else sc(c, 0)))
        return out
    if kind == "zanjian":
        rh = max(0.0, (L - D) / 2)
        t0 = 0.0
        ts = np.linspace(0, 1, K + 1) ** 0.9
        rings = _rings(lambda t: rh + (hx0 - rh) * t, lambda t: hz0 * t, yf, ts, n, up, out_, t0)
        out.append(face_up(_drop_degenerate(_sheet(rings, c))))
        if fascia and detail:
            out.append(_fascia(rings[-1], float(np.clip(0.05 * D, 0.25, 0.9)), TEAL))
        if rh < 0.3:                                 # the gilded finial
            r = float(np.clip(0.05 * D, 0.35, 1.3))
            out.append(lathe([(r * 1.2, 0), (r * 1.3, r * 0.4), (r * 0.5, r * 0.8), (r * 0.9, r * 1.3), (r * 1.0, r * 1.9),
                              (r * 0.6, r * 2.6), (0.0, r * 3.0)], GOLD, 8).T(0, yr - 0.2, 0))
        elif ridge:
            out.append(B(-rh, rh, yr - hr * 0.35, yr + hr * 0.65, -hr * 0.4, hr * 0.4, YELLOW_D))
        return out
    if kind == "wudian":
        rh = min(hx0 - 0.5, max(0.0, (L - D) / 2 + 0.08 * L))   # tuishan: the ridge pushed out
        ts = np.linspace(0, 1, K + 1) ** 0.9
        rings = _rings(lambda t: rh + (hx0 - rh) * t, lambda t: hz0 * t, yf, ts, n, up, out_)
        out.append(face_up(_drop_degenerate(_sheet(rings, c))))
        if fascia and detail:
            out.append(_fascia(rings[-1], float(np.clip(0.05 * D, 0.25, 1.0)), TEAL))
        if ridge:
            rc = YELLOW_D if c == YELLOW else sc(c, 0)
            out.append(B(-rh - hr * 0.3, rh + hr * 0.3, yr - hr * 0.35, yr + hr * 0.65, -hr * 0.4, hr * 0.4, rc))
            if detail >= 2:
                for s in range(4):
                    pts = [R[s * n] + [0, hr * 0.25, 0] for R in rings]
                    out.append(tube(pts, hr * 0.32, rc, 4))
            if chiwen:
                for sx in (-1, 1):
                    out.append(B(sx * (rh + hr * 0.3) - hr * 0.45, sx * (rh + hr * 0.3) + hr * 0.45, yr, yr + hr * 1.8, -hr * 0.3, hr * 0.3, rc))
        return out
    # xieshan: the lower part hipped (45° hips) up to t = tg, then a gable roof with red gables
    rh = hx0 - hz0
    ts = tg + (1 - tg) * np.linspace(0, 1, max(2, K - 1) + 1)
    rings = _rings(lambda t: rh + (hx0 - rh) * t, lambda t: hz0 * t, yf, ts, n, up, out_, tg)
    out.append(face_up(_drop_degenerate(_sheet(rings, c))))
    if fascia and detail:
        out.append(_fascia(rings[-1], float(np.clip(0.05 * D, 0.25, 1.0)), TEAL))
    gx = rh + (hx0 - rh) * tg
    tu = np.linspace(0, tg, max(2, K - 1) + 1)
    xs = np.linspace(-gx - 0.15 * hz0 * tg, gx + 0.15 * hz0 * tg, max(2, n - 1) + 1)
    for sgn in (1, -1):
        V, F = [], []
        for t in tu:
            for x in xs:
                V.append((x, yf(t), sgn * hz0 * t))
        nx = len(xs)
        for k in range(len(tu) - 1):
            for i in range(nx - 1):
                a, b = k * nx + i, (k + 1) * nx + i
                F += [(a, b, b + 1), (a, b + 1, a + 1)]
        out.append(face_up(Mesh(V, F, c)))
    for sx in (1, -1):
        x = sx * (gx - 0.1 * hz0 * tg)
        prof = [(hz0 * t, yf(t)) for t in tu[::-1]] + [(-hz0 * t, yf(t)) for t in tu[1:]]
        V = [(x, yf(tg) - 0.05, 0.0)] + [(x, y - 0.05, z) for z, y in prof]
        F = [(0, i, i + 1) for i in range(1, len(V) - 1)]
        out.append(face_out(Mesh(V, F, gable_c)))
    if ridge:
        rc = YELLOW_D if c == YELLOW else sc(c, 0)
        out.append(B(-gx - 0.1, gx + 0.1, yr - hr * 0.35, yr + hr * 0.65, -hr * 0.4, hr * 0.4, rc))
        if chiwen:
            for sx in (-1, 1):
                out.append(B(sx * gx - hr * 0.45, sx * gx + hr * 0.45, yr, yr + hr * 1.8, -hr * 0.3, hr * 0.3, rc))
        if detail >= 2:
            for s in range(4):
                pts = [R[s * n] + [0, hr * 0.25, 0] for R in rings]
                out.append(tube(pts, hr * 0.3, rc, 4))
    return out


def skirt(L, D, ye, Lu, Du, ys, c, detail=1):
    """The lower roof of double eaves: from the eave rectangle L × D at ye up to the upper body Lu × Du at ys."""
    n = {0: 2, 1: 3, 2: 5}[detail]
    t_in = Du / D
    rh = (Lu / 2 - (L / 2) * t_in) / max(1 - t_in, 1e-3)
    ts = t_in + (1 - t_in) * np.linspace(0, 1, 3)
    up = float(np.clip(0.04 * D, 0.2, 1.4))
    yf = lambda t: ye + (ys - ye) * ((1 - t) / (1 - t_in)) ** 0.8
    rings = _rings(lambda t: rh + (L / 2 - rh) * t, lambda t: (D / 2) * t, yf, ts, n, up, up * 0.6, t_in)
    return [face_up(_sheet(rings, c)), _fascia(rings[-1], float(np.clip(0.04 * D, 0.25, 0.9)), TEAL)]


def body(Lb, Db, y0, y1, col=RED, doors=True, band=True):
    """Red walls and columns of a hall (Lb × Db, from y0 to y1), the painted band under the eaves, lattice doors."""
    out = [walls(rect(-Lb / 2, Lb / 2, -Db / 2, Db / 2), y0, y1, col)]
    h = y1 - y0
    if band and h > 2.2 and Lb > 5:
        bh = min(0.9, 0.18 * h)
        out.append(walls(rect(-Lb / 2 - 0.03, Lb / 2 + 0.03, -Db / 2 - 0.03, Db / 2 + 0.03), y1 - bh, y1, TEAL))
    if doors and h > 2.5 and Lb > 4:
        top = y1 - (min(0.9, 0.18 * h) if band else 0) - 0.35
        for sz in (1, -1):
            V = [(-Lb / 2 + 1.0, y0 + 0.4, sz * (Db / 2 + 0.04)), (Lb / 2 - 1.0, y0 + 0.4, sz * (Db / 2 + 0.04)),
                 (Lb / 2 - 1.0, top, sz * (Db / 2 + 0.04)), (-Lb / 2 + 1.0, top, sz * (Db / 2 + 0.04))]
            out.append(face_out(Mesh(V, [(0, 1, 2), (0, 2, 3)], RED_D)))
    return out


def hall(cx, cz, a, L, D, base, ye, yr, kind, rc=YELLOW, Lb=None, Db=None, plat=None, plat_c=MARBLE, double=None,
         detail=None, chiwen=False, body_c=RED, doors=True):
    """A hall: platform, body, (skirt), roof. L × D = the (lower) eave rectangle along a; base = floor level.
    double = (ys, Lu, Du, ye2, Lt, Dt): skirt up to ys at the upper body Lu × Du, upper eaves Lt × Dt at ye2."""
    if L < D:
        L, D, a = D, L, a + math.pi / 2
        if Lb is not None:
            Lb, Db = Db, Lb
        if double:
            ys, Lu, Du, ye2, Lt, Dt = double
            double = (ys, Du, Lu, ye2, Dt, Lt)
        if plat not in (None, False):
            plat = (plat[1], plat[0])
    if detail is None:
        detail = 2 if D > 24 else (1 if D > 13 else 0)
    o = float(np.clip(0.11 * D, 0.5, 3.2))
    if Lb is None:
        Lb, Db = L - 2 * o, D - 2 * o
    Lb, Db = max(Lb, 1.0), max(Db, 1.0)
    out = []
    if plat is not False and (base > 0.05 or plat):
        Lp, Dp = plat if plat else (Lb + 2 * 0.7 * o + 0.4, Db + 2 * 0.7 * o + 0.4)
        out.append(B(-Lp / 2, Lp / 2, FOUND, base, -Dp / 2, Dp / 2, sc(plat_c, 0.02)))
    if double:
        ys, Lu, Du, ye2, Lt, Dt = double
        Hs = ys - ye
        yb1 = ye + Hs * 0.25
        out += body(Lb, Db, base, yb1, body_c, doors)
        out += skirt(L, D, ye, Lu, Du, ys, rc, detail)
        Hu = yr - ye2
        ou = (Dt - Du) / 2
        yb2 = ye2 + Hu * (max(ou, 0.3) / (Dt / 2)) ** P_EXP
        out += body(Lu, Du, ys - 0.3, yb2, body_c, doors=False)
        out += roof(Lt, Dt, ye2, yr, kind, rc, detail, chiwen=chiwen)
    else:
        H = yr - ye
        yb = ye + H * (o / (D / 2)) ** P_EXP if kind != "gable" else ye + 0.1
        out += body(Lb, Db, base, yb, body_c, doors and detail > 0)
        out += roof(L, D, ye, yr, kind, rc, detail, chiwen=chiwen)
    return [place(m, a, cx, cz) for m in out]


# ── Walls with tiled coping ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
def pwall(p0, p1, h, th=1.3, c=WALL_RED, cop=YELLOW, y0=FOUND):
    """A palace wall from p0 to p1 (x, z), h high, with its yellow-tiled coping."""
    (x0, z0), (x1, z1) = p0, p1
    Lw = math.hypot(x1 - x0, z1 - z0)
    if Lw < 0.3:
        return []
    a = math.atan2(z1 - z0, x1 - x0)
    cx, cz = (x0 + x1) / 2, (z0 + z1) / 2
    out = [B(-Lw / 2, Lw / 2, y0, h - 0.35, -th / 2, th / 2, c)]
    w = th / 2 + 0.35
    V = [(-Lw / 2 - 0.2, h - 0.45, -w), (Lw / 2 + 0.2, h - 0.45, -w), (Lw / 2 + 0.2, h + 0.25, 0), (-Lw / 2 - 0.2, h + 0.25, 0),
         (-Lw / 2 - 0.2, h - 0.45, w), (Lw / 2 + 0.2, h - 0.45, w)]
    m = Mesh(V, [(0, 2, 1), (0, 3, 2), (4, 5, 2), (4, 2, 3), (0, 4, 3), (1, 2, 5)], cop)
    out.append(m)
    return [place(q, a, cx, cz) for q in out]


def balustrade(p0, p1, y, c=MARBLE, h=1.05, step=5.5, posts=True):
    """A marble balustrade from p0 to p1 at level y: a rail and posts."""
    (x0, z0), (x1, z1) = p0, p1
    Lw = math.hypot(x1 - x0, z1 - z0)
    if Lw < 0.6:
        return []
    a = math.atan2(z1 - z0, x1 - x0)
    out = [B(-Lw / 2, Lw / 2, y, y + h * 0.85, -0.13, 0.13, c)]
    if posts:
        n = max(1, int(Lw / step))
        for k in range(n + 1):
            u = -Lw / 2 + Lw * k / n
            out.append(B(u - 0.17, u + 0.17, y, y + h * 1.18, -0.17, 0.17, c))
    return [place(m, a, (x0 + x1) / 2, (z0 + z1) / 2) for m in out]


def ring_edges(P):
    P = [tuple(p) for p in P]
    if ring_area(P) < 0:
        P = P[::-1]
    for i in range(len(P)):
        a, b = P[i], P[(i + 1) % len(P)]
        d = math.hypot(b[0] - a[0], b[1] - a[1])
        if d < 1e-6:
            continue
        nx, nz = (b[1] - a[1]) / d, -(b[0] - a[0]) / d          # outward normal of a counter-clockwise ring
        yield a, b, (nx, nz)


def wedge(P, h, dirv, c):
    """A stair or ramp: the outline P rising from 0 on the downhill side (dirv) to h on the other."""
    P = [tuple(p) for p in P]
    pts, tris = triangulate(P)
    pr = pts @ np.array(dirv)
    lo, hi = pr.min(), pr.max()
    ys = h * (1 - (pr - lo) / max(hi - lo, 1e-6))
    top = Mesh(np.stack([pts[:, 0], ys, pts[:, 1]], 1), tris[:, ::-1], c)
    V, F = [], []
    Q = list(pts)
    for i in range(len(Q)):
        j = (i + 1) % len(Q)
        o = len(V)
        V += [(Q[i][0], FOUND, Q[i][1]), (Q[j][0], FOUND, Q[j][1]), (Q[j][0], max(ys[j], 0.05), Q[j][1]), (Q[i][0], max(ys[i], 0.05), Q[i][1])]
        F += [(o, o + 2, o + 1), (o, o + 3, o + 2)]
    side = Mesh(V, F, sc(c, 0.01))
    cx, cz = pts.mean(0)
    return [face_up(top), face_out(side, cx, cz)]


def bearing_vec(b):
    """A compass bearing (degrees) -> unit vector in model x/z."""
    r = math.radians(float(b) - HEADING)
    return (-math.sin(r), math.cos(r))


# ── The data from OpenStreetMap ──────────────────────────────────────────────
GREEN_ZONE = (235, 335, 5, 62)                 # the Southern Three Lodges (Nansansuo): green tiles
STONE_SCALE = {i: 3.44 / 7.0 for i in (638308768, 638308769, 638308770, 638308771, 638308773, 638308774, 638308775, 638308776)}
STONE_SCALE.update({638329299: 3.44 / 4.0, 638329301: 3.44 / 4.0})
CUSTOM = {638156366, 638741722, 156146468, 156146621, 40343947, 638449347, 638473398, 638308745}
SPEC_S = {}


def roof_colour(name, cx, cz):
    x0, x1, z0, z1 = GREEN_ZONE
    if x0 < cx < x1 and z0 < cz < z1:
        return GREEN_T
    if name == "文渊阁":
        return BLACK_T
    if any(k in name for k in ("平房", "房子", "长房")):
        return GREY_T
    return YELLOW


class Stones:
    def __init__(self, items):
        self.items = []
        for s in items:
            sid, P, h, shape, dirn, col = s[:6]
            holes = s[6] if len(s) > 6 else []
            h = h * STONE_SCALE.get(sid, S_STONE)
            x0, x1, z0, z1 = bbox(P)
            self.items.append(dict(id=sid, P=P, h=h, shape=shape, dir=dirn, col=col, holes=holes, bb=(x0, x1, z0, z1)))

    def level(self, x, z, flat_only=True):
        best = 0.0
        for s in self.items:
            x0, x1, z0, z1 = s["bb"]
            if x0 <= x <= x1 and z0 <= z <= z1 and (not flat_only or s["shape"] != "skillion") and pip(x, z, s["P"]):
                best = max(best, s["h"])
        return best

    def any_at(self, x, z, h_min):
        for s in self.items:
            x0, x1, z0, z1 = s["bb"]
            if x0 <= x <= x1 and z0 <= z <= z1 and pip(x, z, s["P"]):
                if s["shape"] == "skillion" or s["h"] >= h_min - 0.05:
                    return True
        return False

    def meshes(self, extra=()):
        out = []
        for s in self.items + list(extra):
            c = STONE if s["col"] in ("LightGrey", "Grey", "gray") else MARBLE
            if s["shape"] == "skillion" and (s["dir"] or s.get("dirv")):
                dv = s.get("dirv") or bearing_vec(s["dir"])
                out += wedge(s["P"], s["h"], dv, MARBLE_D if c == MARBLE else STONE)
                continue
            out.append(extrude(s["P"], FOUND, s["h"], sc(c, 0.015), holes=s["holes"] if s["holes"] else ()))
            if s["h"] >= 1.8:
                for a, b, n in ring_edges(s["P"]):
                    mx, mz = (a[0] + b[0]) / 2 + n[0] * 0.7, (a[1] + b[1]) / 2 + n[1] * 0.7
                    if self.any_at(mx, mz, s["h"]):
                        continue
                    ia = (a[0] - n[0] * 0.3, a[1] - n[1] * 0.3); ib = (b[0] - n[0] * 0.3, b[1] - n[1] * 0.3)
                    out += balustrade(ia, ib, s["h"], MARBLE)
        return out


def _lr_union(rings, a):
    pts = np.vstack([np.asarray(r, float) for r in rings])
    return lrect(pts, a)


def from_parts(bid, name, ring, parts, stones, out):
    """A building drawn with OSM building:parts: walls, bodies and roof levels -> one hall (single or double eaves)."""
    S = SPEC_S.get(bid, S_OSM)
    pp = []
    for P, mn, h, shape, mat in parts:
        a = axis_of(P)
        cx, cz, L, D = lrect(P, a)
        pp.append(dict(P=P, mn=mn, h=h, shape=shape, mat=mat, a=a, cx=cx, cz=cz, L=L, D=D, area=abs(ring_area(P))))
    wallp = [p for p in pp if p["mn"] == 0 and min(p["L"], p["D"]) <= 3.6 and p["mat"] != "concrete"]
    bodies = sorted([p for p in pp if p["mn"] == 0 and p not in wallp and p["mat"] != "concrete"], key=lambda p: -p["area"])
    roofs = [p for p in pp if p["mn"] > 0 and p not in wallp]
    for p in wallp:
        a = p["a"] if p["L"] >= p["D"] else p["a"] + math.pi / 2
        hl = max(p["L"], p["D"]) / 2
        p0 = (p["cx"] - math.cos(a) * hl, p["cz"] - math.sin(a) * hl)
        p1 = (p["cx"] + math.cos(a) * hl, p["cz"] + math.sin(a) * hl)
        base = stones.level(p["cx"], p["cz"])
        out += pwall(p0, p1, max(base + 2.5, p["h"] * S), th=min(p["L"], p["D"]), y0=FOUND)
    rc = roof_colour(name, *_lr_union([ring], 0)[:2])
    if not roofs:
        for p in bodies:
            generic(p["P"], name, p["h"] * S, None, stones, out, rc)
        return
    if not bodies:
        generic(ring, name, max(p["h"] for p in roofs) * S, None, stones, out, rc)
        return
    bd = bodies[0]
    a = bd["a"]
    cx, cz, Lb, Db = bd["cx"], bd["cz"], bd["L"], bd["D"]
    base = stones.level(cx, cz)
    top = max(roofs, key=lambda p: (p["h"], p["area"]))
    levels = sorted(set(p["mn"] for p in roofs))
    low = [p for p in roofs if p["mn"] == levels[0] and p is not top]
    is_ring = len(low) >= 2 and all(p["shape"] == "skillion" for p in low)
    shape = top["shape"]
    if is_ring:
        _, _, L1, D1 = _lr_union([p["P"] for p in low], a)
        hi_sk = [p for p in roofs if p["shape"] == "skillion" and p["mn"] > levels[0]]
        low_top = max(p["h"] for p in low)
        if hi_sk or top["mn"] - low_top >= 0.9:
            ye1, ys = levels[0] * S, low_top * S
            if hi_sk:
                _, _, Lt, Dt = _lr_union([p["P"] for p in hi_sk], a)
                ye2 = min(p["mn"] for p in hi_sk) * S
            else:
                _, _, Lt, Dt = lrect(top["P"], a)
                ye2 = top["mn"] * S
            ub = [p for p in bodies[1:] if p["h"] > bd["h"]]
            if ub:
                _, _, Lu, Du = lrect(ub[0]["P"], a)
            else:
                Lu, Du = Lt - 0.25 * Dt, Dt * 0.75
            kind = {"hipped": "wudian", "pyramidal": "zanjian"}.get(shape, "xieshan")
            Lu, Du = min(Lu, Lb - 1.0), min(Du, Db - 1.0)
            ye2 = max(ye2, ys + 0.6)
            out += hall(cx, cz, a, max(L1, Lb + 1), max(D1, Db + 1), base, max(ye1, base + 2.5), max(top["h"] * S, ye2 + 2),
                        kind, rc, Lb=Lb, Db=Db, plat=False, double=(ys, Lu, Du, ye2, max(Lt, Lu + 1), max(Dt, Du + 1)),
                        chiwen=D1 > 18)
            return
        kind = {"hipped": "wudian", "pyramidal": "zanjian"}.get(shape, "xieshan")
        out += hall(cx, cz, a, max(L1, Lb + 1), max(D1, Db + 1), base, max(levels[0] * S, base + 2.5), top["h"] * S, kind, rc,
                    Lb=Lb, Db=Db, plat=False, chiwen=D1 > 18)
        return
    _, _, Lt, Dt = lrect(top["P"], a)
    kind = {"hipped": "xieshan", "pyramidal": "zanjian", "gabled": "xieshan" if min(Lt, Dt) >= 10 else "gable"}.get(shape, "xieshan")
    out += hall(cx, cz, a, max(Lt, Lb + 0.8), max(Dt, Db + 0.8), base, max(top["mn"] * S, base + 2.5), top["h"] * S, kind, rc,
                Lb=Lb, Db=Db, plat=False)


def generic(ring, name, H, rshape, stones, out, rc=None, btype=None):
    """A building known only by its outline: a hall on each rectangle of the plan."""
    a = axis_of(ring)
    cx, cz, L, D = lrect(ring, a)
    if rc is None:
        rc = roof_colour(name, cx, cz)
    if min(L, D) <= 3.4:                        # a wall (or a gate in a wall)
        u = a if L >= D else a + math.pi / 2
        hl = max(L, D) / 2
        h = H if H else 6.5
        out += pwall((cx - math.cos(u) * hl, cz - math.sin(u) * hl), (cx + math.cos(u) * hl, cz + math.sin(u) * hl), h, th=min(L, D))
        return
    area = abs(ring_area(ring))
    if area / max(L * D, 1e-6) > 0.82 or len(ring) <= 5:
        rects = [(-L / 2, L / 2, -D / 2, D / 2, cx, cz)]
    else:
        rs = decompose(ring, a)
        rects = []
        for u0, u1, v0, v1 in rs:
            x, z = from_local((u0 + u1) / 2, (v0 + v1) / 2, a)
            rects.append((u0, u1, v0, v1, x, z))
        if not rects:
            rects = [(-L / 2, L / 2, -D / 2, D / 2, cx, cz)]
    small_pav = ("亭" in name) and max(L, D) < 16
    for u0, u1, v0, v1, x, z in rects:
        Lr, Dr = u1 - u0, v1 - v0
        d = min(Lr, Dr)
        if rshape == "pyramidal" or (small_pav and len(rects) == 1):
            kind = "zanjian"
        elif rshape == "gabled":
            kind = "gable"
        elif rshape == "hipped":
            kind = "xieshan"
        else:
            kind = "xieshan" if d >= 10 else "gable"
        if kind == "xieshan" and d < 5.5:
            kind = "gable"
        base0 = stones.level(x, z)
        own = base0 < 0.05
        base = base0 if not own else float(np.clip(0.3 + 0.045 * d, 0.35, 1.3))
        E = float(np.clip(2.6 + 0.2 * d, 3.0, 7.5))
        R = {"gable": 0.3, "xieshan": 0.33, "zanjian": 0.48, "wudian": 0.36}[kind] * d
        if H:
            avail = max(H - base, 2.5)
            k = avail / (E + R)
            E, R = E * k, R * k
        pc = MARBLE if any(t in name for t in ("殿", "宫", "阁", "楼", "门")) else STONE
        out += hall(x, z, a, Lr, Dr, base, base + E, base + E + R, kind, rc, plat=None if own else False, plat_c=pc)


def build_buildings(D, stones):
    out = []
    for bid, name, ring, htag, rshape, btype, relmax, parts in D["b"]:
        if bid in CUSTOM or relmax == -1:            # custom-built, or only marble platforms (drawn as such)
            continue
        try:
            if parts:
                from_parts(bid, name, ring, parts, stones, out)
            else:
                H = float(htag) * S_OSM if htag else None
                generic(ring, name, H, rshape, stones, out, btype=btype)
        except Exception as e:                          # noqa: BLE001
            print("skipped", bid, name, repr(e))
    for wid, line, h, closed in D["bw"]:
        hh = float(h) if h else 5.5
        pts = line + ([line[0]] if closed else [])
        for p0, p1 in zip(pts[:-1], pts[1:]):
            base = stones.level((p0[0] + p1[0]) / 2, (p0[1] + p1[1]) / 2)
            out += pwall(p0, p1, base + hh, th=1.1)
    return out


# ── The city wall, its corner towers and gates ───────────────────────────────
SW, SE, NE, NW = (-376.24, 485.09), (375.73, 477.40), (375.73, -484.83), (-375.22, -477.66)
WALL_Q = [SW, SE, NE, NW]           # the outer face of the wall (OSM ways 638176319, 1341826249, 638252480, 1341826250)
WALK = 8.4                          # the wall walk
PARA = 9.3                          # top of the outer parapet; the merlons reach 10.0


def ring3(Q, d, y):
    return np.array([(x, y, z) for x, z in offset(Q, -d)])


def city_wall():
    out = []
    o0, o1, o2 = ring3(WALL_Q, 0, FOUND), ring3(WALL_Q, 0.05, 1.3), ring3(WALL_Q, 0.85, WALK)
    out.append(face_out(_sheet([o0, ring3(WALL_Q, 0, 1.3)], STONE)))
    out.append(face_out(_sheet([ring3(WALL_Q, 0.05, 1.3), o2], WALL_RED)))
    i0, i2 = ring3(WALL_Q, 8.6, FOUND), ring3(WALL_Q, 7.6, WALK)
    m = face_out(_sheet([i0, ring3(WALL_Q, 8.6, 1.0)], STONE)); m.f = m.f[:, ::-1]; out.append(m)
    m = face_out(_sheet([ring3(WALL_Q, 8.55, 1.0), i2], WALL_RED)); m.f = m.f[:, ::-1]; out.append(m)
    out.append(cap(offset(WALL_Q, -0.85), WALK, BRICK, holes=[offset(WALL_Q, -7.6)]))
    # outer crenellated parapet and the low inner parapet
    out.append(face_out(_sheet([ring3(WALL_Q, 0.85, WALK - 0.02), ring3(WALL_Q, 0.85, PARA)], WALL_RED)))
    m = face_out(_sheet([ring3(WALL_Q, 1.45, WALK), ring3(WALL_Q, 1.45, PARA)], WALL_RED)); m.f = m.f[:, ::-1]; out.append(m)
    out.append(cap(offset(WALL_Q, -0.85), PARA, BRICK, holes=[offset(WALL_Q, -1.45)]))
    out.append(face_out(_sheet([ring3(WALL_Q, 7.0, WALK), ring3(WALL_Q, 7.0, WALK + 0.9)], WALL_RED)))
    m = face_out(_sheet([ring3(WALL_Q, 7.6, WALK), ring3(WALL_Q, 7.6, WALK + 0.9)], WALL_RED)); m.f = m.f[:, ::-1]; out.append(m)
    out.append(cap(offset(WALL_Q, -7.0), WALK + 0.9, BRICK, holes=[offset(WALL_Q, -7.6)]))
    R = offset(WALL_Q, -1.15)
    for i in range(4):
        (x0, z0), (x1, z1) = R[i], R[(i + 1) % 4]
        Lw = math.hypot(x1 - x0, z1 - z0)
        a = math.atan2(z1 - z0, x1 - x0)
        n = int((Lw - 30) / 3.2)
        for k in range(n):
            u = 15 + (k + 0.5) * (Lw - 30) / n
            out.append(place(B(-0.95, 0.95, 0, 0.7, -0.3, 0.3, WALL_RED).T(u - Lw / 2, PARA, 0), a, (x0 + x1) / 2, (z0 + z1) / 2))
    return out


def arch(cx, y0, w, h, facing, pos, c=DARK):
    """A dark arched opening (a tunnel through a gate platform) on a face: facing '+z', '-z', '+x', '-x' at pos."""
    seg = 6
    r = w / 2
    pts = [(-r, 0), (r, 0), (r, h - r)] + [(r * math.cos(t), h - r + r * math.sin(t)) for t in np.linspace(0, math.pi, seg + 1)[1:-1]] + [(-r, h - r)]
    V = [(u, y0 + v, 0.0) for u, v in pts]
    F = [(0, i, i + 1) for i in range(1, len(V) - 1)]
    m = Mesh(V, F, c)
    if facing == "+z":
        m.T(cx, 0, pos + 0.06)
    elif facing == "-z":
        m.R(0, math.pi, 0).T(cx, 0, pos - 0.06)
    elif facing == "+x":
        m.R(0, math.pi / 2, 0).T(pos + 0.06, 0, cx)
    else:
        m.R(0, -math.pi / 2, 0).T(pos - 0.06, 0, cx)
    return m


def red_platform(P, h, parapet=True):
    out = [extrude(P, FOUND, h, WALL_RED, top_c=BRICK)]
    out.append(walls(offset(P, 0.05), FOUND, 1.2, STONE))
    if parapet:
        Q = offset(P, -0.15)
        out.append(walls(Q, h - 0.02, h + 1.0, WALL_RED))
        Qi = offset(P, -0.75)
        out.append(walls(Qi, h, h + 1.0, WALL_RED, hole=True))
        out.append(cap(Q, h + 1.0, BRICK, holes=[Qi]))
    return out


def corner_tower(cx, cz):
    """A jiaolou on its bastion: cross plan, porches with gables on four sides, two crossing hip-and-gable roofs."""
    out = []
    y0 = WALK + 0.35 + 1.3
    out.append(B(cx - 7.9, cx + 7.9, WALK + 0.3, y0, cz - 7.9, cz + 7.9, MARBLE))           # sumeru base
    out += [place(m, 0, cx, cz) for m in body(8.2, 8.2, y0, y0 + 9.2, RED, doors=False)]
    for k in range(4):
        a = k * math.pi / 2
        loc = []
        loc.append(B(4.0, 6.9, y0, y0 + 4.4, -3.3, 3.3, RED))
        loc.append(B(4.0, 6.95, y0 + 3.7, y0 + 4.4, -3.35, 3.35, TEAL))
        for m in roof(5.4, 8.6, y0 + 4.4, y0 + 7.6, "gable", YELLOW, 1, up=0.5):
            loc.append(m.T(5.5, 0, 0))
        out += [place(m, a, cx, cz) for m in loc]
    out += [place(m, 0, cx, cz) for m in skirt(11.6, 11.6, y0 + 4.5, 8.2, 8.2, y0 + 6.4, YELLOW, 1)]
    out += [place(m, 0, cx, cz) for m in skirt(10.6, 10.6, y0 + 7.4, 8.2, 8.2, y0 + 8.6, YELLOW, 1)]
    for a in (0, math.pi / 2):
        out += [place(m, a, cx, cz) for m in roof(12.6, 8.0, y0 + 9.2, y0 + 15.4, "xieshan", YELLOW, 1, chiwen=False)]
    out.append(lathe([(0.75, 0), (0.85, 0.3), (0.35, 0.7), (0.6, 1.1), (0.55, 1.6), (0.0, 2.1)], GOLD, 8).T(cx, y0 + 15.3, cz))
    return out


def corner_towers():
    out = []
    centres = []
    for (x, z), (sx, sz) in ((SE, (-13.2, -13.9)), (NE, (-14.5, 14.0)), (SW, (13.2, -13.9)), (NW, (14.5, 14.0))):
        cx, cz = x + sx, z + sz
        centres.append((cx, cz))
        out.append(B(cx - 13.6, cx + 13.6, FOUND, WALK + 0.35, cz - 13.8, cz + 13.8, WALL_RED))
        out.append(B(cx - 13.65, cx + 13.65, FOUND, 1.3, cz - 13.85, cz + 13.85, STONE))
        out += corner_tower(cx, cz)
    return out


